<title>AUSTRALIA: Soccer-Venables maintains perfect record.</title>
<headline>Soccer-Venables maintains perfect record.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia thrashed Tahiti 5-0 in an Oceania group World Cup qualifying match on Friday to maintain Terry Venables' perfect record since becoming national coach last year.</p>
<p>Australia have maximum points from two games after routing Solomon Islands 13-0 on Wednesday and appear certain to cruise into a play-off to decide the Oceania winners.</p>
<p>South Melbourne striker Paul Trimboli, one of nine changes made by Venables to the starting line-up on Friday, scored twice in the match at Parramatta Stadium.</p>
